From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 11:34:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(web): cover the theme style tables and the material
 layer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`theme-styles.test.ts` now walks every entry of THEME_STYLES and asserts the
per-style metadata, the derived `<html>` class list, a palette for each style
(light + dark for the non-forced-dark ones, anchored so `.dark.blueprint`
cannot satisfy the plain `.blueprint` check), the resolved naive-ui colours and
the label key in all 11 locales — adding a style without its palette or locale
key now fails the suite instead of rendering as ink.

Also pins the material layer: every ambient block must be scoped to a style
class, and a user background image must clear `.app-layout`'s texture, and the
app shell theme mock exposes the `style` ref the shell now reads.

`normalizeThemeStyle` used to be asserted with `'neon'` as an unknown value;
`neon` is a real style now, so the sample moved to `'vaporwave'`.

`style-system.test.ts` and `theme-customization.test.ts` follow the renamed
`StylePalette` / `styleOverrides` exports.
